{
  "version": 1,
  "_comment": "Keybindings. Every entry here feeds ~/.config/hypr/keybinds.conf (or hyprland/keybinds.lua in Lua mode), the Keybindings page in the GUI, and the SUPER+F1 help screen. The user can override a keybinding with KEYBINDS in settings.conf: KEYBINDS=\"terminal=MOD+T;;lock=MOD+CTRL+L\" — an empty value removes that keybinding entirely.",
  "_note_end4": "Key combos are aligned with the end-4/dots-hyprland defaults (illogical-impulse, commit 2f0c8bf). end-4's quickshell-specific keybindings (OSK, Google Lens, OCR, translation, media panel, wallpaper picker, VM submap) were not taken over because this project has no equivalent; those with a close equivalent were mapped: SUPER tap = launcher, SUPER+A = Actions (instead of the left sidebar), SUPER+N = notification center, SUPER+G = widgets, SUPER+J = bar, SUPER+CTRL+R = reload Hyprland (restarts the shell there). Deliberate deviations: SUPER+Tab (overview there) is next workspace here since there is no overview; SUPER+C (code editor there) centers the window here; SUPER+ALT+R/G stay with Instant Replay; ALT+Tab is this project's window switcher. Project-specific additions use keys unused in end-4: SUPER+ALT+T split direction, SUPER+ALT+arrows resize, SUPER+ALT+N night light, SUPER+F1 help.",
  "_schema": {
    "id": "stable id (used in KEYBINDS overrides)",
    "title": "name shown in the UI and on the help screen",
    "keys": "MOD+SHIFT+L format; the MOD, SHIFT, CTRL, ALT tokens are joined with '+'",
    "dispatcher": "Hyprland dispatcher (exec, killactive, movefocus…) — translated to an hl.dsp.* call automatically in Lua mode",
    "args": "dispatcher argument; {{VARIABLE}} placeholders are filled in at render time",
    "flags": "'' | e (repeat) | l (also when locked) | el | m (mouse)",
    "require": "the require syntax from the templates; if the condition is not met, no line is generated",
    "editable": "if false, it cannot be reassigned in the UI (mouse/wheel bindings)"
  },
  "_note_dispatchers": "Dispatcher names can change between Hyprland versions. In 0.54 'togglesplit' and 'swapsplit' were removed; they are now called via 'layoutmsg' (see https://hypr.land/news/update54/). When adding a keybinding, verify the name against https://wiki.hypr.land/Configuring/Dispatchers/; a wrong name gives an 'Invalid dispatcher' error when Hyprland starts. './install.sh --doctor' catches these errors via 'hyprctl configerrors'. In Lua mode (HYPR_LANG=lua) every dispatcher is turned into an hl.dsp.* call from the translation table in python/hyprsetup/keybinds.py; those without an entry run as-is via 'hyprctl dispatch'.",
  "categories": [
    {
      "id": "apps",
      "title": "Applications",
      "binds": [
